---
title: "Cultural Anthropology"
code: "SOC-211"
category: "sociology"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Examines the origins, development, research, diversification and evolution of human cultures. Includes exposure to the variability of both Western and Non-Western aspects of culture. Provides an introduction to the nature of culture and its relationship to various social institutions and societies. This is a Passport Transfer course. Lecture 3 hours per week.
